  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {道|みち}を{辿|たど}る: to follow a road/path\n- {記憶|きおく}を{辿|たど}る: to trace one's memories\n- {歴史|れきし}を{辿|たど}る: to trace history\n- {同|おな}じ{道|みち}を{辿|たど}る: to follow the same path (figurative: to have the same fate)\n- {運命|うんめい}を{辿|たど}る: to follow a fate/course\n\nUSAGE: Implies a sense of deliberateness or difficulty in the journey. Often used figuratively for intellectual or emotional processes of tracing back through something.",
